---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import { prizes, works, portraits } from '../lib/catalogue';
import { downloadsFor } from '../lib/downloads';
import { href } from '../lib/links';
const articles = await getCollection('awards');
const workArticles = await getCollection('works');
const published = articles.filter(a => a.data.status === 'published').length;
const drafts = articles.filter(a => a.data.status !== 'metadata-only' && a.data.status !== 'published').length;
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial coverage ledger"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">An honest accounting</p><h1>A complete catalogue.<br/><em>A growing body of research.</em></h1><p>Catalogue coverage and editorial completion are different measures. This ledger is derived from the actual records at build time.</p></header><div class="coverage-stats"><div><strong>{prizes.length}</strong><span>official award records</span></div><div><strong>{published}</strong><span>published, reviewed essays</span></div><div><strong>{drafts}</strong><span>editorial drafts / in progress</span></div><div><strong>{works.length}</strong><span>evidence-linked works</span></div></div><div class="prose"><h2>What remains</h2><p>{prizes.length-published} annual essays still require research or editorial review. {portraits.length} portraits have verified permissions. Original-paper files are linked externally unless a specific version has distribution clearance. Draft exports demonstrate the document pipeline and are not completed research.</p><p>Editorial status is never inferred from page existence or word count. A named review record and valid exports are required for publication. See the <a href="https://github.com/willtheorangeguy/econ-nobel/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION_PROGRESS.md">implementation progress</a> for engineering and QA limitations.</p></div><h2>Year-by-year ledger</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Award coverage table"><table class="ledger"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Editorial state</th><th scope="col">Linked works</th><th scope="col">Overview exports</th></tr></thead><tbody>{prizes.map(p => { const article = articles.find(a => a.id === String(p.year))!; const files = downloadsFor('awards',String(p.year)); return <tr><th scope="row"><a href={href(`awards/${p.year}/`)}>{p.year}</a></th><td><Status status={article.data.status}/></td><td>{article.data.featured_work_ids.length}</td><td>{files.length ? `${files.map(f => f.format.toUpperCase()).join(' + ')}${article.data.status !== 'published' ? ' (draft)' : ''}` : 'Not yet available'}</td></tr>; })}</tbody></table></div><h2>Work explanation coverage</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Work explanation coverage table"><table class="ledger"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Work</th><th scope="col">Editorial state</th><th scope="col">Overview exports</th></tr></thead><tbody>{works.map(w=>{const a=workArticles.find(a=>a.id===w.id)!;const files=downloadsFor('works',w.id);return <tr><th scope="row"><a href={href(`works/${w.id}/`)}>{w.title}</a></th><td><Status status={a.data.status}/></td><td>{files.length?`${files.map(f=>f.format.toUpperCase()).join(' + ')} (draft)`: 'Not yet available'}</td></tr>;})}</tbody></table></div></BaseLayout>
